course: dictionary
lesson: 15619
title: Who is a taxpayer?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A taxpayer is a person or business that pays tax. Tax is money paid to the government. «Every taxpayer helps to pay for the new school.» Ask yourself who pays, and the answer is the taxpayer.
explain: Tax money pays for things we all use, like schools, hospitals, roads, police and parks. «The new bridge was built with taxpayers' money.» The bridge belongs to everyone, so everyone who pays tax helps to build it.
explain: Look at the apostrophe. «Taxpayers' money» means money from many taxpayers, so the apostrophe comes after the s. «At the taxpayer's expense» means one taxpayer, so the apostrophe comes before the s.
fact: Taxpayer is a noun. One taxpayer, many taxpayers.
fact: «Taxpayer» means a person or business that pays tax to the government.
fact: Tax is money that people and businesses pay to the government.
fact: Taxes help pay for schools, hospitals, roads, police and parks.
fact: «Taxpayers' money» means money that comes from the people who pay tax.
exercise: «Every taxpayer helps pay for the new school.» What is a taxpayer? | *A person or business that pays tax to the government | A builder who makes roads | A shop that sells school bags | A teacher who works at the school
exercise: «The new park was paid for with taxpayers' money.» Where does this money come from? | From the ice cream van | From the children's pocket money only | *From people and businesses who pay tax | From the trees in the park
exercise: Which of these is paid for with taxes? | A sweet shop on the corner | A birthday cake for one family | A football kit for one player | *A hospital for the whole town
test: What does «taxpayers' money» mean? | Money found on the ground | Money that a bank has lost | *Money from the people who pay tax | Money won in a game
test: Which spelling shows the money of many taxpayers? | taxpayers money | taxpayer's money | *taxpayers' money | taxpayer money
exam: What is the plural of taxpayer? | *taxpayers | taxpayer | taxpayerses | taxpayer's
